    "result": "**No defects found in this diff.**\n\nIt renames the private field `_repository` to `_invoices` and the constructor parameter `repository` to `invoices` in `ApprovalService.cs`. Every `_repository` reference in the hunks (the constructor, three `Update` calls and `Find`) was changed, and nothing else changed. The behavior is the same, so the rename can't alter the Draft → PendingApproval → Approved/Rejected lifecycle.\n\nI only reviewed the diff, not the full file or the rest of the repo. There are two things I didn't check:\n- **A missed `_repository` reference:** a use outside the shown hunks would fail to compile, so the build would catch it.\n- **A named-argument caller:** code calling `new ApprovalService(repository: ...)` would also fail to compile. That's unlikely, since `Program.cs` uses dependency injection and the tests would normally pass the fake positionally.\n\nRunning `dotnet test backend/InvoiceApp.sln` would settle both. My confidence that the change is correct is high, about 95%.",
